# membres.ttl — the collective's side of the handshake (solid-kit ADR 006 §2).
#
# Descriptive only: it grants NOTHING. Rights stay in the .acl files, one
# WebID at a time.
#
# Two kinds of lines, both facts the collective owns:
# - foaf:member, under the collective's IRI from config.ttl (not a local
#   <#mapsofmaking>, which would be a different IRI);
# - foaf:nick, the short name the collective uses in depots/ and
#   confrontations/ paths. Set at acceptance, never changed once used.
# Names and agents are NOT copied here: they are read from each profile.
#
# Empty at creation: the backoffice adds both lines when a request is
# accepted, for example:
# <config.ttl#mapsofmaking> foaf:member <https://pod.example/alice/profile/card#me> .
# <https://pod.example/alice/profile/card#me> foaf:nick "alice" .

@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
